
==============================================================================
[1] does the model fit a real burn at all?  (23 fires)
==============================================================================
    IoU of the fitted final front with the observed one: median 0.376, p25 0.227, p75 0.462
    for scale, section 3 found the best area-matched ellipse reaches a median
    IoU of 0.705 on real final perimeters, so this is the ceiling to beat.

==============================================================================
[2] does the answer depend on where the fit started?
==============================================================================
    Each fire was fitted three times, from 1.5, 3.0 and 6.0 m/s -- a 4x span.
    ratio of largest to smallest fitted wind, per fire: median 25.45x, p90 29.74x
    ratio of largest to smallest final misfit:          median 1.9206x, p90 2.7856x
    fires where the three fits stay more than 1.5x apart: 91 %

    If the burn determined the wind, the three fits would converge on one
    answer and only one of them would fit well. A spread in the answers with
    no spread in the misfit is the degeneracy, on real fires.

==============================================================================
[3] is the recovered wind right?
==============================================================================
    wind speed, relative error against GRIDMET: median 94 %, p25 88 %, p75 95 %
    wind bearing, absolute error: median 29 deg, p25 15, p75 56
    fires whose bearing lands within 45 deg: 65 %; a random bearing would give 25 %

==============================================================================
[4] does the guard know it cannot have the wind speed?
==============================================================================
    wind speed called determined: 0 % of fires
    wind bearing called determined: 26 %

    Sections 1 and 13 say a burn mask cannot give the speed and can give
    the bearing on flat ground. The guard is applied to real fires with no
    knowledge of either, and its verdicts are what they are.

==============================================================================
[5] separating 'not identifiable' from 'the model does not fit'
==============================================================================
    On real fires those two explanations are confounded, and the honest way to
    look at it is to ask whether the fires the model *does* fit behave any
    differently. If the wind pins down where the fit is good, the failure is
    misspecification; if it does not, misspecification is not the explanation.

           fit quality   fires   median U spread   median U error   bearing err
            IoU < 0.38      11             26.6x              93 %           29d
           IoU >= 0.38      12             23.8x              94 %           35d

